Tomasz, Yolanda,<br />
<br />
Agreed on the undertaking, and I want to put the reasoning somewhere findab=
le because this question is going to come up again on other files.<br />
<br />
An undertaking given to the staff is a promise in the terms in which it is =
written. The 2012 letter identifies its subject by schedule: 103 enumerated=
 accounts, reconciled to a billing system as of a date in 2012. It contains=
 no forward-looking clause and no language about accounts subsequently acqu=
ired or onboarded. Nothing in it can be read to reach a client relationship=
 that did not exist when it was signed. Counsel drafted it that way deliber=
ately, the examiner recorded that she understood it that way, and the staff=
 accepted it on those terms.<br />
<br />
So the Sewickley accounts have to stand or fall on the rule. That is not a =
weaker case; in some ways it is a cleaner one, because it does not require =
us to prove up a 2012 document at all. It is simply a different case, and t=
he theory has to be stated correctly from the outset.<br />
<br />
What I do not want to see is a referral memorandum that leads with the 2012=
 undertaking and treats the account population as an afterthought. That get=
s the pleading wrong and hands the firm an easy first motion.<br />
<br />
Gretchen Sallenave<br />
